/target
# Python bytecode from the anchor/golden DRIVER scripts under crates/*/tests. Importing one
# (as the K3 tokenizer verification did) leaves a .pyc that is build output, not source — it
# was staged once on 2026-08-17 before this line existed.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# session/tooling artifacts that live in the working dir, never in the repo
.claude/pruned-patches/
.claude/settings.local.json
.snapshot_path

# HARNESS RUNTIME STATE, versioned here rather than only in `.git/info/exclude` (added
# 2026-08-31, review). `.claude/` became repo content in this commit — settings.json, the
# hook, the agent defs, the skills — and every pattern below was ignored ONLY by the local
# exclude file, which is per-clone machine state and is never cloned. So on the first fresh
# clone or worktree, `git add .claude` would sweep in live agent mailboxes, checkpoints and
# registry state; `.claude/worktrees/` here already holds two complete checkouts, which git
# would stage as mode-160000 gitlinks — two pseudo-submodules pointing at branch tips, and
# `git ls-files -o` reports nothing there, so the mistake would be invisible in `status`.
# The local exclude keeps its copies (ignoring is idempotent); these are the ones that travel.
**/.claude/worktrees/
**/.claude/checkpoints/
**/.claude/mailbox/
**/.claude/routines/.state/
**/.claude/agent-registry.json
**/.claude/agent-memory-local
**/.claude/scheduled_tasks.json
**/.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
**/.claude/assistant-daemon-state.json
**/.claude/first-run
